            <ArticleTitle>Thoracic intradural Aspergillus abscess formation following epidural steroid injection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>642-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report an extremely unusual iatrogenic infection of the spinal canal with Aspergillus fumigatus that resulted in intradural abscess formation following epidural steroid injection in an immunocompetent young individual. Although the imaging findings of the infection were relatively nonspecific, MR imaging not only allowed for a prompt diagnosis, but also helped in surgical localization to the intradural compartment. Complications from the use of these injections are briefly discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
